# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RF0 deny-by-default boundary (2026-10-04).
#
# Nothing is tracked unless it is re-included below, so a blanket `git add`
# can never sweep in the game assets (3.0 GB), the export corpus, a 100 MB
# evidence dump or a bin/obj tree. The excluded heavy/volatile files are NOT
# lost -- they stay in place and are associated with the baseline by SHA256 in
# _dpsm_work/baseline-manifest.json (see REPO-BOUNDARY.md).
#
# Rule of thumb: this file answers "what may a commit contain", the boundary
# document answers "why is X out".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- root: deny every entry, then re-include the tracked entry documents ---
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/REPO-BOUNDARY.md
!/DpsMeter-文档索引.md
!/DpsMeter-使用说明-完整版.txt
!/安装说明.txt
!/changelog.txt
!/dpsmeter_analyze.py
!/dpsmeter_contrib.py
!/_dpsm_work/

# --- the live plugin config is small text and IS part of the baseline ---
!/BepInEx/
/BepInEx/*
!/BepInEx/config/
/BepInEx/config/*
!/BepInEx/config/dev.dpsmeter.cfg

# --- _dpsm_work: work products only; heavy dumps stay out ---
/_dpsm_work/*
!/_dpsm_work/*.py
!/_dpsm_work/*.md
!/_dpsm_work/*.txt
!/_dpsm_work/*.json
!/_dpsm_work/*.cfg
!/_dpsm_work/src/
!/_dpsm_work/tests/
!/_dpsm_work/recon_probe/
!/_dpsm_work/test/
!/_dpsm_work/contrib/
!/_dpsm_work/contrib_cs/
!/_dpsm_work/review_contrib_core/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_1.7.11/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf2/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf3/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf4/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf4b/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf4c/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf5a/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf4d/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf7a/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf4e/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf5b/
!/_dpsm_work/acceptance_rf5c/

# Derived, multi-MB analysis outputs inside a batch archive. They are reproducible from the frozen
# snapshot by the tracked tools, so the archive keeps its EVIDENCE (RESULTS.md, corpus_manifest.json,
# runs.json, applicability.json, the guard transcripts) and not a 4 MB re-derivation: committing them
# made one round 155,906 inserted lines for a 5 MB artifact. acceptance_1.7.11 (round 6) predates this
# rule and stays complete as history; the files remain on disk either way.
/_dpsm_work/acceptance_*/pairtrusted_impact_report.json
/_dpsm_work/acceptance_*/pairtrusted_impact_report.txt

# Scratch files under tests/ (commit messages, throwaway harnesses). tests/ is re-included above, so
# without this rule a `git add -A` picks a temporary file up and the next commit deletes it again.
/_dpsm_work/tests/_*.tmp

# --- derived output / caches, anywhere ---
bin/
obj/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# --- heavy or volatile inputs and artefacts (recorded by hash, not tracked) ---
BepInEx/plugins/
BepInEx/interop/
BepInEx/core/
BepInEx/LogOutput.log
BepInEx/config/dpsmeter_runtime.log*
rlyehshoujotaix_cl_Data/
D3D12/
dotnet/
DpsMeter-0.9.0-r2/
汉化/
*.zip
*.dll
*.exe
*.bak
